1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,362
This video shows you how to connect smeltr to a GitHub repository,

2
00:00:06,362 --> 00:00:09,990
so your team reviews and merges changes on GitHub.

3
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,674
Here's the team's repository on GitHub.

4
00:00:12,674 --> 00:00:13,630
It's empty.

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:17,622
In smeltr, open Admin, System, Git remote.

6
00:00:17,622 --> 00:00:21,319
Enter the repository's clone URL.

7
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:27,195
Add a GitHub token that can read the repository and push to it.

8
00:00:27,195 --> 00:00:30,710
smeltr stores it encrypted, and never shows it again.

9
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:33,856
Fetch every minute, and save.

10
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:39,454
The repository was empty, so smeltr pushes its main there.

11
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:44,634
On GitHub, main now holds your routes and pipelines.

12
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:55,135
In Sam's browser, Sam keeps the message as it came,

13
00:00:55,135 --> 00:00:58,670
and removes the assignment that uppercases it.

14
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:06,620
Sam saves on a branch of their own, and opens it for review.

15
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:17,990
Every save goes to GitHub, on a branch of the same name.

16
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:22,986
While Approve: pushes to main is off, changes are merged on GitHub,

17
00:01:22,986 --> 00:01:26,230
so smeltr doesn't deploy this one itself.

18
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:29,429
On GitHub, open a pull request from the branch.

19
00:01:29,429 --> 00:01:33,244
Your team reviews it there, like any other code.

20
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:38,548
When it's merged, main moves.

21
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:43,595
smeltr fetches main every minute.

22
00:01:43,595 --> 00:01:48,722
It checks that every worker group loads the new commit, then deploys it.

23
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:53,064
Status shows the fleet on the new commit.

24
00:01:53,064 --> 00:01:58,270
A commit that doesn't load leaves the fleet where it was, and Status says why.

25
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,196
Check on learning.

26
00:02:00,396 --> 00:02:03,195
smeltr follows a GitHub repository.

27
00:02:03,195 --> 00:02:05,795
Where is a change merged?

28
00:02:10,195 --> 00:02:11,030
On GitHub.

29
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:16,136
smeltr pushes each save to a branch, and deploys main.

30
00:02:17,036 --> 00:02:19,312
A commit on main doesn't load.

31
00:02:19,312 --> 00:02:21,732
What does the fleet run?

32
00:02:26,132 --> 00:02:28,021
The last commit that did.

33
00:02:28,021 --> 00:02:31,265
Status says why the new one didn't.

34
00:02:32,165 --> 00:02:38,074
Next, you approve changes in smeltr, and smeltr pushes them to GitHub's main.
